<p>
<font size=5>Phase III Design Process: Teamwork is the Key</font><br>
<b>UI Eco-Hydraulics Group (UI)</b>
<p>
<img src="key-team.jpg" width=150 height=63 align="right">
The UI team presented Phase III design ideas at the TAC meeting on Sept. 8th and appreciated the discussion and comments from all those in attendance.  This input will be addressed in the preparation of the design materials for the Nov. 10th TAC meeting in Lewiston.
<p>
Steve Clayton contacted Nick Gerhardt (USFS), and Nick agreed to provide the UI team with data for 1986-97 water years for three gauges:  Trapper Creek, South Fork Red River, and Main Fork Red River.  The UI team will use this information to develop flows for the models used in the design process.  Nick also will provide the UI team with information from bedload studies in the area.  Steve Bauer is providing UI with streamflow and water quality data from the past few field seasons.
<p>
The UI team, under the guidance of Tony Minns, has initiated modeling of the Red River on the WMA property.  Gloria Beattie has formatted all the survey data (through Sept.) and she and Tony have input the data into the Mike 11 Model.  Cross-section survey data collected on site from 1994 and 1997 will be compared to the model's predictions.  Survey data collected in October 1998 will also be incorporated into the model as quickly as feasible.  With the hydrologic, bedload, and channel cross section information, the team will use the model to test various planforms, cross section dimensions, and gradients.  We will use this information to develop a conceptual design that will facilitate the return of the stream to a state of dynamic equilibrium, self-sustaining over time. 

